    <string name="about_privacy">Privacy policy</string>
    <string name="privacy_policy_text">This policy explains how the Speed Contact app handles your data.\n\nDeveloper: CDIT, Creative Development &amp; IT Programming, Khamis Mushait, Saudi Arabia. Contact: email info@cdit.co, phone and WhatsApp +966502010911, or the contact form at cdit.co.\n\nData the app accesses\n• Contacts: names, nicknames, phone numbers, photos and the favorite mark, to show people in your widgets. It reads them again in the background to update the widgets when they change.\n• Making calls: to start a call when you tap a person. The app does not read your call log.\n• Gallery pictures: only the picture you choose as a folder icon.\n\nUse and storage\nAll processing happens on your phone. The app has no internet permission, so it sends no data to the developer or anyone else, and it contains no ads or analytics. In its private storage it keeps your widget settings, the people and numbers you chose, the time of the last call started from its widgets for each person, and a small copy of an icon picture. This data is not included in cloud backups.\n\nSharing\nWe do not share your data with anyone. When you choose a text message, WhatsApp or the contact card, that app opens and receives the number or contact to carry out your request, and its own policy then applies.\n\nDeletion\nA widget\'s settings are deleted when you remove it from the home screen, and all stored data is deleted when you uninstall the app. The app never changes or deletes your contacts. You can withdraw any permission in your phone\'s settings at any time.\n\nChildren\nThe app is not directed at children under 13.\n\nChanges\nAny change to this policy is published here. Last updated: 9 November 2026.</string>
